{"type":"standard","title":"Yukulta language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Yukulta language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3913765","titles":{"canonical":"Yukulta_language","normalized":"Yukulta language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Yukulta language</span></span>"},"pageid":31494319,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Wellesley_Islands_locator_map.jpg/330px-Wellesley_Islands_locator_map.jpg","width":330,"height":298},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/Wellesley_Islands_locator_map.jpg","width":1500,"height":1355},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1343094594","tid":"9596eade-1dd9-11f1-9ef3-4730aa6a858d","timestamp":"2026-03-12T06:06:18Z","description":"Extinct Australian Aboriginal language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yukulta_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yukulta_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yukulta_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Yukulta_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yukulta_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Yukulta_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yukulta_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Yukulta_language"}},"extract":"The Yukulta language, also spelt Yugulda, Yokula, Yukala, Jugula, and Jakula, and also known as Ganggalidda, is a Tangkic language spoken in Queensland and Northern Territory, Australia. It was spoken by the Yukulta people, whose traditional lands lie on the southern coast of the Gulf of Carpentaria.","extract_html":"<p>The <b>Yukulta language</b>, also spelt <b>Yugulda</b>, <b>Yokula</b>, <b>Yukala</b>, <b>Jugula</b>, and <b>Jakula</b>, and also known as <b>Ganggalidda</b>, is a Tangkic language spoken in Queensland and Northern Territory, Australia. It was spoken by the Yukulta people, whose traditional lands lie on the southern coast of the Gulf of Carpentaria.</p>"}